    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.pick\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nWhen `content_from_bottom` is enabled, mini.pick swaps title and footer [here](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.pick/blob/be6490ae9d7038b9f5185d95a8060054f9b23666/lua/mini/pick.lua#L2587). Since the footer is built with the bottom border char as filler [here](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.pick/blob/be6490ae9d7038b9f5185d95a8060054f9b23666/lua/mini/pick.lua#L2606), the wrong character is being used.\n\nI can submit a PR with a fix. There are multiple ways to handle this but I guess that can be discussed in the PR.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n`init.lua`:\n\n```lua\nvim.pack.add({\n  \"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\n})\nlocal border = { \"\", \"─\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \" \", \"\", \"\" }\nrequire(\"mini.pick\").setup({\n  options = { content_from_bottom = true },\n  window = {\n    config = {\n      border = border,\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThen run `:=MiniPick.builtin.files()` or similar.\n\n<img width=\"1278\" height=\"1378\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dc25fe8d-caa0-4636-8f10-3aea0d4e4d6d\" />\n\nYou can see the configured top border char in the top left corner, but the bottom border char is used as a filler.",
